# Halcyon's leaders, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): 0 the job, 1 the
# built news, 2 what they make of you, each carried by a topic. Voice: precise, a bit cold,
# sometimes guilty. Humour only by accident. Halcyon talks in numbers.
# Work talk explains the work (what, where, who for, the pay, the danger) before the accept.

conv halcyon.leader.work_samples
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
when need:samples
topic "What is the count short of?"
prio ask
voice halcyon

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? stronghold :: Tissue. Fresh, from the infected, under six hours old. We have three usable samples this week. We need eleven.
  say? trait:idealist :: Samples. I know what that word sounds like to you. It's the only word that gets us to the cure.
  say Samples. The work stops without them, and the work can't stop: the incubators run on a schedule, not on what we happen to have.
  say We're at {cure_percent} percent. Every point costs something that used to walk, and we buy the points one sample at a time.
  > @what What sort of samples? -> what
  > @who Samples from whom, exactly? -> whose
  > @worth What do I get for them? -> worth
  > @lab Your chain of custody is a mess. -> custody   if bg:labtech,doctor,nurse
  > @help Is there work in it for me? -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node what
  say Blood, tissue, a sample of the fluid behind the eye. The unusual ones are best: the ones that run, or scream. We provide the kit. You provide the nerve.
  say Sealed, labelled, cold. Under six hours, or it's a souvenir.
  > @help2 I can do cold. -> offer
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node whose
  say The dead ones. The infected. Nobody living, if that's your question. It's always the first question.
  say? major:proof :: The second question is the one the Haven keeps asking, about our volunteers. Ask it somewhere else, please.
  say It's a fair question. I'd ask it.
  > @help3 Then I'll bring them in. -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node worth
  say? trait:greedy :: Favor. A place in the queue for the first doses. The queue is the only thing in the Zone that's worth more every day.
  say Halcyon Favor, which buys antiseptic and stabilisers at our stores, and antidotes when we have them. And our gratitude, which we record. In triplicate.
  > @help4 Triplicate it is. -> offer
  > @back3 Let me think about it. -> hub

node custody
  say It is. Two of my four field staff can't spell contaminated. You can, apparently.
  say Bring them sealed and dated, and I'll stop apologising to the director.
  > @help5 Then let me bring them in properly. -> offer
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node offer
  say It's fieldwork. You go into an infested town, kill what you have to, and bring us tissue in a sealed case. Or carry a case between a station and the lab, or guard someone taking readings.
  say It pays Halcyon Favor, and it moves the number. Infested towns are infested for a reason. Most of what we'll ask you to kill was a person once, and still runs like one.
  > @take I'll do it. Give me the kit. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @risk What's the risk, honestly? -> risk
  > @later Let me think about it. -> hub

node risk
  say Bites, mostly. Sample work is close work. If you're bitten, the trial dose is free, once, and eight in ten walk out. So, conditionally, the risk is two in ten.
  say I've been told that's a cold way to put it. The Red Hand buy samples too, and they don't like competition on the road.
  > @take4 Understood. I'll do it. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later4 Not today, then. -> hub

node other_route
  say You've committed to another route for the cure. It's in your file. The file doesn't stop us using you, and the work pays the same.
  > @take2 Is there work for me anyway? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say? cure_held:halcyon :: We hold the cure. The work now is making enough of it, and deciding who's first. The second part isn't science.
  say The cure exists. The work isn't finished. It's never finished. It's just less urgent, and the barriers stay closed until processing.
  > @take3 Then I'll keep working for you. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.work
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
when !need:samples
topic "What does the lab need?"
prio ask
voice halcyon

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? need:security :: Guards. The lab has two doors and four guards. One of the doors doesn't lock. I've stopped writing that down.
  say? need:supplies :: Reagents, filters, generator fuel. If the power drops for forty minutes, two weeks of cultures die.
  say? need:people :: Hands. Clean ones. The volunteers are not staff, whatever the rota says.
  say Time. We need time, and the only way to buy it is people bringing us things.
  say? stand :: The lab is holding its final stand. Every door has someone at it. One percent at a time, under fire.
  say? cure>=90 :: We're past ninety. Everyone wants to be in the room when it finishes. Nobody wants to be in the room if it doesn't.
  say? finale:open :: And four factions want the cure to belong to them. We'd like it to work first.
  say We're at {cure_percent} percent. The last ten are the slowest. They always are.
  > @why Why is it taking so long? -> slow
  > @risk What happens if the power goes? -> power
  > @press What aren't the numbers saying? -> told | partial | partial   check persuade halcyon 2 harder:paranoid bg:labtech,doctor
  > @help Give me something to do. -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node slow
  say Because every step is a test, and every test is a person, or a part of one. We go as fast as the dead allow, and they don't hurry for anyone.
  > @help2 Then let me speed it up. -> offer
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node power
  say We lose two weeks of cultures. Possibly three. We'd survive. Some of the cultures would not. Neither, possibly, would I.
  say The generator takes diesel, and diesel comes from the Red Hand or out of Bastion's stores. Neither sells it to us cheaply.
  > @help3 Then let me keep it running. -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node told
  say The trial doses. One in three of the new batch takes. That's an improvement. The other two are also a number.
  say I'd like you to remember both.
  do learn:halcyon.one_in_three:6h
  > @help4 I'll remember. What can I do? -> offer
  > @back3 I'll remember. Something else. -> hub

node partial
  say The numbers are saying everything. You're not listening to all of them. Neither is anyone else.
  > @help5 Then give me work instead. -> offer
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node offer
  say There's tasking: fuel and a generator part for the lab, a crashed drone's core, sensors placed in infested towns, a hard drive out of a dead clinic. Each one is described exactly.
  say It pays Halcyon Favor, and some of it moves the cure. Please read the description exactly. People who skim it come back with the wrong part, or don't come back.
  say? trait:ruthless :: The form was short. So is the margin for error.
  > @take I'll do it. What's first? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later Let me think about it. -> hub

node other_route
  say You've committed to another route for the cure. It's in your file. The file doesn't stop us using you, and the work pays the same.
  > @take2 Is there work for me anyway? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say The cure exists. The rest is logistics, and grief, and paperwork about both. The barriers stay closed until processing.
  > @take3 Then give me some paperwork. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.news
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
topic "What do the radio logs say?"
prio world
voice halcyon

bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind horde = news:horde
bind over = news:overrun
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by

node start
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:overrun -> overrun
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:taken -> taken
  say? epilogue :: The logs say processing at the road checkpoints. Ninety-one percent of the messages since are people asking what processing means.
  say? edge :: The logs say the drones over the line flew their usual pattern. Fourteen passes a day. We counted. Counting is calming.
  say? outbreak:overrun :: The logs say the infected are adapting faster than we are. That's a measurement, not an opinion.
  say The logs say what they always say. Forty messages a day on the open channel, six worth keeping. We read our own numbers out at every shift change, in case anyone outside is writing them down.
  > @mine What does your file say about me? -> me
  > @more Anything else in the logs? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back0 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node dead
  say {bind:dead} is dead. I've added the name to a list. We keep a lot of lists.
  say? trait:idealist :: It shouldn't feel like a statistic. It does. I'm sorry for that, not that it helps anyone.
  > @more1 What else is in the logs? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node overrun
  say {bind:over} has passed eighty on our infection index. That's what we call overrun when we're being polite.
  say If you're going there, take a sample kit. If you're not going there, good.
  > @more2 What else is in the logs? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node horde
  say A group of them moved near {bind:horde}. Somewhere between forty and sixty, by the noise. They follow sound.
  say Somebody ran a generator. Generators are the dinner bell of the modern age.
  > @more3 What else is in the logs? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node taken
  say {bind:who} holds {bind:took} now. It changes nothing for the lab. It changes everything for the people there.
  > @more4 What else is in the logs? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  say? best:halcyon :: That you {best}. Noted, with a date. Dates are how we say thank you.
  say? symptoms :: That you're symptomatic. That's in the file in red. Red means come and see us before the end, not after.
  say A file with your name on it and two lines of notes. Two is more than most people get.
  > @back5 Good to know. Something else. -> hub

node me_colours
  say That you came in wearing another faction's clothes. Recorded as an observation, not a judgement.
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.me
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
topic "How would you file me?"
prio reaction
voice halcyon

node start
  jump kit:other -> colours
  jump bite_shown -> bitten
  jump tier:halcyon>=trusted -> trusted
  jump tier:halcyon>=known -> known
  say? fresh :: New. One page, most of it blank. Blank is not a bad result. It means nothing has gone wrong yet.
  say Subject: unaffiliated. Usefulness: not yet measured. That's not an insult. It's a column, and the column is empty.
  > @more And what's in the column now? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @fair Fair. -> hub

node colours
  say You're wearing someone else's colours in a sterile area. That's two problems. I've ranked them.
  > @more1 And otherwise, where do I stand? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node bitten
  say Bite visible. Under twelve hours, by the colour. You know where the lab is. I'd prefer you came in walking.
  say? declared :: You told a house. That's in your favour, in the file and otherwise.
  > @more2 Am I still welcome here? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 I'll come to the lab. -> hub

node trusted
  say? title:halcyon :: Staff call you {title:halcyon}. They don't name anyone. Two of them argued about it for a day.
  say Reliable. That's the highest word we use. It sounds small. In here it's a medal.
  > @more3 Can I see the full file? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back3 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node known
  say? jobs:halcyon>=3 :: Three tasks, completed to specification. Statistically, you're a pattern.
  say Known to the lab. The guards will use your name. They'll still check your hands.
  > @more4 And where do I stand overall? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub
